# Sigma Computing POC — Evaluation Plan, Criteria & Rubric

**Prepared for:** Sigma POC (Snowflake + Databricks connections), compared against MicroStrategy / Strategy ONE (MSTR)
**Doc check date:** October 21, 2026 (Sigma features and beta status change often; re-check links before the readout)

---

## 0. Instructions for Claude (project context)

- Use this file as the source of truth for the Sigma POC evaluation criteria, test steps, and scoring.
- Every product claim in a readout must cite **official documentation**: Sigma (help.sigmacomputing.com), Snowflake (docs.snowflake.com), Databricks (docs.databricks.com), Strategy/MSTR (Strategy product help, community KB, release notes).
- Always state whether a Sigma feature is **GA, public beta, or private beta**. Beta features score no higher than 2 unless the team accepts beta risk in writing.
- Do not invent license prices. Sigma license cost is **vendor quote required**. Third-party estimates (Vendr, Querio, etc.) may be shown only as "indicative, not verified."
- Keep answers precise and in tables when comparing tools.

