## 2. Doc-Verified Facts That Shape This POC

These come from official Sigma docs. Each one drives a specific test below.

| # | Fact | Impact on POC | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| F1 | Tables **cannot be joined across connections** in Sigma. | No Snowflake ↔ Databricks join inside Sigma. | [Joins overview](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/joins-overview) |
| F2 | **Write access** (a writable schema/catalog) is required for **materialization, CSV uploads, input tables, and warehouse views**. | If prod disallows table creation, all four features are unavailable. Hard dependency. | [Connect to data sources](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/connect-to-data-sources), [Set up write access](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/connections) |
| F3 | Materialization writes a copy of the data back to the warehouse as a table (or Snowflake dynamic table) in the Sigma-managed write-back schema. | Sigma's closest equivalent to an MSTR cube — but it creates warehouse objects. | [About materialization](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/materialization) |
| F4 | Materialization status: datasets and data model elements are **GA**; workbook elements are **public beta**. | Score workbook-level materialization as beta. | Same as F3 |
| F5 | Materialization **fails** if data uses a system function, such as row-level security. Tagged workbook versions cannot be materialized. Controls targeting a materialized element query live data. | RLS + materialization do not combine. Version-tagged prod workbooks can't be materialized (data models can). | Same as F3 |
| F6 | Materialization queries ignore the Sigma connection timeout and use the warehouse's own timeout. | Heavy transforms depend on warehouse timeout settings. | Same as F3 |
| F7 | Caching order: browser cache → Alpha Query → warehouse query ID cache (Snowflake/BigQuery only) → universal result cache (beta) → re-query. Manual or scheduled refresh bypasses all caching. | Databricks has no query ID cache in Sigma; relies on live queries or beta universal cache. | [Caching and data freshness](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/caching-and-data-freshness) |
| F8 | On **OAuth** connections, the query ID cache and universal result cache are only used when the workbook **runs with service account credentials**. | Trade-off: per-user identity pass-through (OAuth) vs. caching/performance. Must test both. | Same as F7 |
| F9 | Universal result cache is **public beta**, not supported for Snowflake (uses native cache), and needs an **external storage integration**. | For Databricks, caching needs a new cloud storage object — check if allowed. | [Manage universal result cache](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/manage-universal-result-cache) |
| F10 | RLS is set up with user attributes (`CurrentUserAttributeText`). Docs note the RLS filter can be modified by anyone viewing the table it is applied on; apply it only directly on an element. | Must prove viewers cannot bypass RLS. Consider warehouse-native RLS (UC row filters, Snowflake row access policies) via OAuth instead. | [Set up row-level security](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/row-level-security) |
| F11 | Databricks + OAuth is the method for per-user Unity Catalog permissions. Write access needs `MODIFY` and `CREATE TABLE` on dedicated write catalogs/schemas. | Confirms write access = new objects in UC. | [Connect to Databricks](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/connect-to-databricks) |
| F12 | Version tags support Dev/Test/Prod workflows, source swapping, and protected tags. Git integration is through the REST API. | SDLC is tag-based, not branch-based. | [Version tagging](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/add-version-tags-to-workbooks-and-data-models) |
| F13 | **Data models as code** (JSON/YAML via v2 API) is available. **Workbooks as code** is private beta. | CI/CD possible for data models; workbooks need beta access. | [Manage data models as code](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/manage-data-models-as-code) |
| F14 | Most exports are limited to **1 million rows** (CSV/Excel); PDF tables max 1,000 rows per table; cloud storage exports are not limited. | Check against large MSTR report exports/subscriptions. | [Download and export limitations](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/docs/download-export-and-upload-limitations) |
| F15 | Snowflake semantic views can be browsed and queried in Sigma (**beta**, Oct 2025). Databricks lists Sigma among BI tools that can query UC metric views. | Option to reuse warehouse semantic layers. Verify current status. | [Sigma release notes Oct 10, 2025](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/changelog/2025-10-10), [UC metric views](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/metric-views/) |
| F16 | AI: Ask Sigma renamed **Sigma Assistant** (Apr 2026); AI context for data models (beta); Sigma MCP server; AI providers include warehouse models, OpenAI, Azure OpenAI, Gemini, Amazon Bedrock (May 2026); AI columns for Databricks (Jun 2026). | AI features depend on the AI provider your org approves. | [Release notes Apr 17, 2026](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/changelog/2026-04-17), [Changelog](https://help.sigmacomputing.com/changelog) |
| F17 | Audit log is a connection (Admin-only by default); usage dashboards and audit log hold **90 days** by default. | Check retention vs. compliance needs. | [Sigma usage data and logs](https://www.sigmacomputing.com/product-faq/how-to-use-sigmas-usage-data-and-logs) |
