## 3. Scoring Rubric

| Score | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 5 | Fully meets the requirement natively, GA, no workaround |
| 4 | Meets with minor configuration |
| 3 | Partially meets; workaround needed |
| 2 | Meets only via beta feature or significant workaround |
| 1 | Does not meet |
| N/A | Not testable in POC (e.g., vendor-withheld info, blocked by constraint) — document reason |

- **Weighted score** = Σ (score × weight) / Σ (weights of scored items)
- **Gate rule:** a score of 1 on any **Gate** criterion = POC fail, regardless of total.
- **Beta cap:** a criterion met only through a beta feature scores max 2 unless beta risk is accepted in writing.
- **Constraint rule:** a feature that needs write access is scored "Blocked by constraint" if prod disallows table creation.

